WEBVTT

00:00.480 --> 00:10.610
Tsuki no kaasu tsumetai yume no naka de

00:00.480 --> 00:10.610
Under the moon’s curse, inside of a cold dream…

00:19.120 --> 00:25.500
Kotoba no nai sekai de bokura wa ai wo kataru

00:19.120 --> 00:25.500
In a world without words, we speak of love

00:25.500 --> 00:29.460
itsuka kimi ni todoku made

00:25.500 --> 00:29.460
until it reaches you someday.

00:32.300 --> 00:39.180
Kizu darake no kaina de dakiyoseta kuchibiru no

00:32.300 --> 00:39.180
I want to melt the frozen over wish...

00:39.180 --> 00:44.850
haritsumeta negai tokashitakute

00:39.180 --> 00:44.850
from the lips that I embraced with arms covered in wounds.

00:45.100 --> 00:51.820
Nee, aishiatta kako no utsukushisa sutesareba

00:45.100 --> 00:51.820
Hey, if I abandon the beauty of the past when we loved each other,

00:52.190 --> 00:57.990
ashita motto kirei na yoru e yukeru kara

00:52.190 --> 00:57.990
then tomorrow, I can go to a more beautiful night.

00:58.370 --> 01:06.540
Tsuki no kaasu tsumetai yume no naka kara

00:58.370 --> 01:06.540
Under the moon’s curse, from inside of a cold dream.

01:06.540 --> 01:13.210
Kimi wo tooku tsuresaritakute

01:06.540 --> 01:13.210
I want to take you somewhere far away,

01:13.210 --> 01:16.630
doko made yukeru

01:13.210 --> 01:16.630
and go anywhere,

01:16.630 --> 01:24.230
ai wo shinjite ii basho made

01:16.630 --> 01:24.230
to a place where we can believe in love.

01:33.780 --> 01:37.030
Natsumi, who do you love
more, Mommy or Daddy?

01:37.260 --> 01:38.830
Mommy's number 1, right?

01:38.830 --> 01:41.300
Um, umm...

01:41.300 --> 01:44.450
Both are number 1!
I love Mommy and Daddy!

01:44.820 --> 01:46.320
I see. I see.

01:48.380 --> 01:49.570
Love...

01:50.970 --> 01:54.130
What does it mean?

01:54.780 --> 01:56.340
"Love..."

01:56.680 --> 01:58.720
I love you, Ritsuka.

01:59.350 --> 02:02.470
I really love it when you smile!

02:02.470 --> 02:05.380
I like the current Ritsuka.

02:07.020 --> 02:08.340
I don't know why...

02:09.110 --> 02:12.940
I should be happy,
but my heart gets cold.

02:14.570 --> 02:18.700
When Soubi says it, it just hurts...

02:25.670 --> 02:26.830
Ritsuka!

02:28.500 --> 02:29.790
Want to join the arts and crafts club?

02:30.480 --> 02:32.430
W-What is it all of a sudden?

02:32.430 --> 02:34.720
Wait a minute. Isn't that a girl's club?

02:34.720 --> 02:35.760
Why me?

02:36.100 --> 02:39.890
Cause, Wednesdays are for
extracurricular activities.

02:39.890 --> 02:42.050
You should do something too!

02:42.050 --> 02:43.250
I'm okay.

02:43.250 --> 02:44.940
Huh? Why?

02:44.940 --> 02:47.020
I'm in the arts and crafts club.

02:47.020 --> 02:49.900
Look, look! I made all this!

02:49.900 --> 02:52.010
I told you, no thanks!

02:52.990 --> 02:54.570
How about the music club?

02:54.970 --> 02:59.700
Right now, we're looking
for accordion players!

02:59.910 --> 03:01.820
Wow! Accordion!

03:01.820 --> 03:02.740
Cool, huh?

03:02.740 --> 03:04.830
Hey, don't decide arbitrarily!

03:04.830 --> 03:06.950
Aoyagi, what do you think
about the English club?

03:07.250 --> 03:09.500
I'm the advisor. It'll be fun.

03:09.900 --> 03:11.420
Teacher, he can't!

03:11.420 --> 03:13.630
He's going to join the music club!

03:12.040 --> 03:13.630
Um, I'm not joining any clubs...

03:13.630 --> 03:16.840
But I'm inviting him to the arts and crafts club!

03:16.840 --> 03:18.590
T-That's a girl's club...

03:19.510 --> 03:21.050
I'm not joining any clubs.

03:21.510 --> 03:22.470
Aoyagi!

03:23.470 --> 03:25.410
Guys stick together!

03:25.410 --> 03:28.220
Let's perform the harmony of friendship!

03:28.220 --> 03:30.690
Aoyagi! Go with the English club.

03:30.690 --> 03:33.230
I'll teach you step by step.

03:33.230 --> 03:36.650
I'll teach Ritsuka step by step, too!

03:36.650 --> 03:37.230
What?

03:37.510 --> 03:40.320
It's okay. I told you I'm
not joining any clubs...

03:40.320 --> 03:41.570
You're mega-stupid!

03:41.960 --> 03:45.160
Yuiko, let's just leave him alone.

03:45.160 --> 03:47.670
We've already made such an effort.

03:47.670 --> 03:48.960
But...

03:48.960 --> 03:49.870
Instead...

03:49.870 --> 03:53.080
I'll join the arts and crafts club.

03:54.710 --> 03:56.630
Y-Yuiko...

03:56.630 --> 03:57.800
No thank you!

03:57.800 --> 04:00.510
Don't be like that.
Teach me step by step too!

04:00.510 --> 04:02.760
Teacher! Yayoi's being gross!

04:02.970 --> 04:03.970
Gross!

04:06.220 --> 04:08.810
Aoyagi! It's your fault!

04:08.810 --> 04:12.270
You didn't decide
fast enough, so Yuiko...

04:12.270 --> 04:14.150
Yuiko...

04:14.940 --> 04:16.940
I'm not joining any clubs.

04:16.940 --> 04:17.820
What?

04:17.820 --> 04:19.950
Don't act like
you didn't hear me the first time!

04:19.950 --> 04:20.530
Why?

04:23.870 --> 04:26.160
I have somewhere to go on Wednesdays.

04:26.160 --> 04:27.740
Oh, Ritsuka!

04:29.540 --> 04:31.200
Did I do something wrong?

04:31.200 --> 04:32.710
You did nothing wrong!

04:34.960 --> 04:37.670
I couldn't tell them the truth.

04:38.970 --> 04:42.720
I see my therapist on Wednesdays...

04:42.720 --> 04:45.800
I've been pushing away my
friends by telling them that.

04:47.850 --> 04:49.260
Excuse me!

04:52.310 --> 04:52.980
No...

04:54.480 --> 04:57.520
Did I even have friends?

05:07.830 --> 05:08.970
Ritsuka.

05:09.620 --> 05:10.710
Soubi!

05:10.710 --> 05:11.660
What do you want?

05:12.170 --> 05:13.840
I just wanted to see you.

05:13.840 --> 05:14.330
Is that bad?

05:16.880 --> 05:18.560
I-It's fine, but...

05:18.560 --> 05:21.260
...I don't have time to
hang around with you today.

05:21.260 --> 05:22.590
Why?

05:22.590 --> 05:24.170
I need to go somewhere.

05:24.970 --> 05:26.180
I'll go with you.

05:26.180 --> 05:27.520
You don't need to.

05:27.520 --> 05:28.470
Actually, don't come!

05:50.000 --> 05:52.330
Hey, about that memo.

05:53.750 --> 05:56.000
You really know something
about it, don't you?

05:57.710 --> 05:59.960
Sorry, I really don't know.

06:00.700 --> 06:05.190
Somebody from "Septimal
Moon" sent me that message!

06:05.720 --> 06:10.180
It could be a trap, but I
have no other leads right now.

06:10.850 --> 06:14.190
Unless you tell me everything you know!

06:14.190 --> 06:15.270
The bus is late.

06:16.190 --> 06:20.540
In any case, think about
what that memo means!

06:21.030 --> 06:22.570
You have a short fuse.

06:22.570 --> 06:23.940
You!

06:26.870 --> 06:28.530
Look, that's your homework!

06:28.820 --> 06:30.110
Don't get on!

06:44.340 --> 06:46.890
It's tiring to be with him.

06:46.890 --> 06:49.800
Natsumi, who do you love
more, Mommy or Daddy?

06:49.800 --> 06:51.770
Mommy's number 1, right?

06:51.770 --> 06:54.100
Um, umm...

06:54.100 --> 06:55.390
Both are number 1!

06:55.390 --> 06:57.600
I love Mommy and Daddy!

06:58.940 --> 07:00.560
You look well, Ritsuka.

07:01.110 --> 07:03.300
I'm tired.

07:03.300 --> 07:05.910
Isn't that because
every day is packed with enjoyment?

07:05.910 --> 07:07.420
Not even.

07:08.120 --> 07:12.030
Ritsuka, you might be skeptical, but...

07:12.350 --> 07:14.660
...I can tell.

07:14.660 --> 07:16.910
You are a perfectly decent
and wonderful kid.

07:16.910 --> 07:18.870
Decent? Me?

07:18.870 --> 07:19.290
Yes.

07:20.090 --> 07:25.710
Say... Today, talk to me instead
of answering my questions.

07:25.930 --> 07:26.920
What?

07:26.920 --> 07:30.130
I'd love to hear you talk.

07:30.130 --> 07:32.850
Talk about what?

07:32.850 --> 07:34.510
Anything's fine.

07:36.190 --> 07:37.360
I...

07:41.150 --> 07:44.620
I think about life, often.

07:44.620 --> 07:45.690
Life?

07:47.110 --> 07:49.310
What do we live for?

07:49.740 --> 07:50.900
Why are we here?

07:51.910 --> 07:57.440
The real Ritsuka from two years ago,
according to Mom, will come back soon.

07:59.130 --> 08:02.140
When that happens,
I'll probably disappear.

08:03.170 --> 08:06.300
So it's meaningless to be here now.

08:07.380 --> 08:11.360
What's important is
the past, the memories...

08:12.310 --> 08:15.090
My future is only to disappear.

08:16.140 --> 08:20.270
Ritsuka, it's just not you
who will disappear someday.

08:20.900 --> 08:22.750
Everyone disappears someday.

08:23.190 --> 08:24.920
You mean, die?

08:24.920 --> 08:26.300
Sure.

08:26.300 --> 08:29.480
But many things disappear
while we're alive, too.

08:30.240 --> 08:33.490
Even for me, I was in grade
school a long time ago...

08:33.780 --> 08:36.780
...but I hardly remember
anything from back then.

08:37.870 --> 08:41.870
I still have pictures and videos,
but I'll never be able to go back.

08:43.170 --> 08:46.770
In other words, the grade
school version of me disappeared.

08:47.170 --> 08:49.430
And the middle school version of me...

08:49.430 --> 08:51.340
...as well as myself from high school.

08:52.260 --> 08:55.430
Even the me from five minutes
ago won't come back.

08:56.270 --> 08:57.800
They've all disappeared.

08:58.890 --> 09:01.720
Then, are the past or
memories meaningless?

09:02.270 --> 09:09.330
I'm not saying it's meaningless.
What's important is to live...

09:09.330 --> 09:14.400
...every moment between now and
when you disappear with all you have.

09:14.400 --> 09:15.930
Isn't that what life is?

09:17.750 --> 09:18.740
But...

09:19.910 --> 09:21.450
But I still don't get it.

09:22.830 --> 09:25.010
Why are people born?

09:25.880 --> 09:27.420
Why do we have to live?

09:28.000 --> 09:28.880
Why?

09:30.340 --> 09:32.060
Why do people die?

09:32.840 --> 09:34.770
He's so young.

09:34.770 --> 09:36.140
What a pity.

09:36.560 --> 09:39.350
Don't tell me that
adults don't know either?

09:44.770 --> 09:46.020
Say, Ritsuka...

09:47.570 --> 09:50.800
It's a little early, but let's
call it a day, and go on a date!

09:50.800 --> 09:51.480
Date?

09:51.740 --> 09:53.780
I'll buy you anything you like.

09:54.490 --> 09:57.540
But I have a curfew...

09:57.540 --> 09:58.860
You'll be okay.

09:59.130 --> 10:00.830
I'll drive you home!

10:06.500 --> 10:09.960
So, do you want Western
food or Japanese?

10:11.260 --> 10:13.250
U-Um, either one!

10:14.390 --> 10:16.630
I'll take three of these.

10:16.630 --> 10:18.290
Thank you.

10:19.970 --> 10:22.900
Yikes, I'm getting nervous.

10:23.480 --> 10:25.370
Bringing gifts for a house call...

10:25.370 --> 10:27.010
Maybe I'm better off without it.

10:27.480 --> 10:30.640
I hope I don't trouble Aoyagi's parents.

10:31.030 --> 10:32.980
What if they get annoyed?

10:34.980 --> 10:43.700
(Sign: Aojima)

10:35.360 --> 10:37.370
This isn't Aoyagi, huh?

10:37.370 --> 10:40.200
Maybe we had to go left at that corner.

10:40.200 --> 10:41.380
Really?

10:41.380 --> 10:43.200
This is getting on my nerves!

10:43.680 --> 10:45.080
What an annoying dog.

10:45.080 --> 10:46.660
Yeah, really!

10:51.090 --> 10:52.420
I just need to get going.

10:54.420 --> 10:56.650
I can't tell on the phone...

10:57.140 --> 11:01.010
I'm sure I can do something
as his homeroom teacher!

11:01.640 --> 11:03.430
Hey, miss.

11:04.560 --> 11:06.480
You know where Aoyagi's place is?

11:06.480 --> 11:07.980
Ritsuka Aoyagi's...

11:08.300 --> 11:11.480
Oh, are you Aoyagi's friends?

11:11.690 --> 11:13.130
Friends?

11:13.130 --> 11:14.550
Did you hear that, Natsuo?

11:14.550 --> 11:16.220
I did, Youji.

11:16.220 --> 11:17.400
Friends, huh?

11:19.030 --> 11:22.030
Miss, you're an adult
but still have your ears.

11:23.500 --> 11:25.080
I-It's not funny.

11:25.080 --> 11:26.630
This is fine as is!

11:27.170 --> 11:29.310
Every person has a different pace.

11:29.310 --> 11:30.890
I'm going at my own pace!

11:32.510 --> 11:34.400
You're funny!

11:34.400 --> 11:36.480
Yeah, funny, I like you!

11:37.680 --> 11:40.800
What are these kids,
making fun of adults!

11:41.220 --> 11:43.470
I'm not interested in older people.

11:44.230 --> 11:46.460
Geez, what am I thinking?

11:46.460 --> 11:48.430
Hey, tell me your name.

11:48.430 --> 11:49.360
What?

11:49.360 --> 11:51.220
Your name.

11:51.570 --> 11:52.900
It's Shinonome, but...

11:52.900 --> 11:55.310
How about your first name?

11:55.310 --> 11:56.550
Hitomi...

11:56.550 --> 11:59.190
Well, cute name...

11:59.190 --> 12:00.300
...Hitomi.

12:00.300 --> 12:00.990
Hey!

12:01.220 --> 12:03.630
Hitomi, I've taken control of your name!

12:04.620 --> 12:06.910
You are a prisoner. I've captured you.

12:06.910 --> 12:08.490
What are you saying?

12:08.490 --> 12:09.500
Return them to me.

12:11.170 --> 12:14.960
What? I can't move my hands and feet!

12:16.220 --> 12:19.070
This is a game. You will be ours.

12:20.590 --> 12:22.010
What did you do to me?

12:22.270 --> 12:23.650
You'll find out soon.

12:23.650 --> 12:26.220
Come on, Hitomi, follow
us with your own legs.

12:26.580 --> 12:28.390
My legs are moving by themselves.

12:28.390 --> 12:30.270
Isn't it great, Hitomi?

12:30.270 --> 12:32.540
You can be a true adult in a bit.

12:32.540 --> 12:36.290
We're ready to get rid
of our ears anytime.

12:36.290 --> 12:38.360
Don't you want them off too?

12:38.740 --> 12:41.280
Mind your own business!

12:41.280 --> 12:44.020
And address me as Miss Shinonome!

12:44.020 --> 12:46.280
I'm older than you, and you just met me!

12:57.340 --> 12:58.590
How about here?

12:59.300 --> 13:01.550
Sounds good to me. Nobody's around.

13:02.260 --> 13:06.470
I don't know what you're
doing, but this isn't fair!

13:06.470 --> 13:08.130
Fair?

13:08.130 --> 13:09.930
I hate fairness.

13:09.930 --> 13:12.140
There's nothing fair about anything.

13:12.140 --> 13:15.320
Don't you know that
this world is irrational?

13:15.320 --> 13:17.150
Fine, I'll teach you!

13:17.150 --> 13:18.900
I command you, Hitomi!

13:19.740 --> 13:22.340
Well, this is awkward.

13:24.990 --> 13:26.200
It's too much trouble, but...

13:26.610 --> 13:30.780
...if I look away and get busted
later, Ritsuka will be angry.

13:30.780 --> 13:32.040
Agatsuma!

13:33.660 --> 13:35.000
Soubi Agatsuma?

13:35.790 --> 13:38.450
And you? Name yourselves.

13:38.450 --> 13:39.470
Natsuo.

13:39.470 --> 13:40.550
Youji.

13:40.550 --> 13:42.170
We're Zero.

13:42.840 --> 13:44.880
These guys are Zero?

13:45.510 --> 13:47.890
Agatsuma, why are you here?

13:48.520 --> 13:50.850
Just killing time.

13:51.390 --> 13:52.100
Teach.

13:56.190 --> 13:57.250
Hey!

13:58.610 --> 14:00.900
It's time for children to go home to bed.

14:00.900 --> 14:02.610
C-Children?

14:02.610 --> 14:05.100
Stop intervening, Soubi Agatsuma!

14:05.100 --> 14:06.660
That's our woman.

14:07.330 --> 14:09.070
Forget about that immature woman.

14:09.620 --> 14:11.100
Immature?

14:11.100 --> 14:13.810
Did he just say immature?

14:14.210 --> 14:15.830
He's younger than I am!

14:15.830 --> 14:18.360
Hey! That's so rude!

14:18.360 --> 14:19.170
Sleep!

14:21.220 --> 14:22.630
It's none of your business.

14:23.200 --> 14:27.260
What do you mean,
none of my business...

14:30.560 --> 14:32.010
Agatsuma...

14:32.690 --> 14:36.850
Why do you always say hurtful things?

14:37.440 --> 14:40.060
Am I saying hurtful things?

14:40.060 --> 14:42.560
You are...

14:43.740 --> 14:44.750
Sorry.

14:46.530 --> 14:48.070
Sentou system, on!

14:53.870 --> 14:56.200
I declare this to be a battle of spells.

14:56.790 --> 14:57.910
I accept.

14:58.500 --> 15:00.550
You're gonna do it by yourself?

15:00.550 --> 15:02.450
Don't you need Loveless?

15:02.840 --> 15:05.450
If the names differ, you
have half your strength.

15:05.450 --> 15:08.250
Without a Sacrifice, another half.

15:08.760 --> 15:11.340
Are you aware of that and
still willing to fight?

15:12.180 --> 15:13.100
Please be gentle.

15:13.100 --> 15:14.640
You're annoying!

15:14.640 --> 15:16.010
Yeah, annoying!

15:16.010 --> 15:18.280
It's a good thing Ritsuka isn't here.

15:18.280 --> 15:19.730
Zero is dangerous.

15:19.730 --> 15:20.770
Shatter!

15:34.330 --> 15:36.260
Maybe you don't like it?

15:36.260 --> 15:38.660
Were we better off
going to a Western place?

15:38.660 --> 15:41.250
Not at all, it's good.

15:41.250 --> 15:43.280
Oh, good.

15:45.090 --> 15:48.170
You know, I recently had
a chance to try burdock root.

15:48.680 --> 15:53.720
Although it was pasta with burdock
in it, I was surprised I liked it.

15:53.720 --> 15:55.850
Wow, pasta with burdock?

15:55.850 --> 15:57.580
That's an unusual dish.

15:57.580 --> 15:59.680
Did your mom make it for you?

16:02.110 --> 16:02.850
No...

16:03.440 --> 16:08.360
If Mom made that,
I'd be too afraid to eat it.

16:09.530 --> 16:11.780
Mom sometimes makes things that I...

16:12.450 --> 16:17.900
That her real Ritsuka hates...

16:17.900 --> 16:19.710
...to test me.

16:21.250 --> 16:24.250
If I eat it, I'll be in big trouble.

16:28.100 --> 16:30.220
I ate it with my friends!

16:30.220 --> 16:31.640
Oh, friends?

16:31.640 --> 16:34.200
That's great! What kind of friends?

16:36.430 --> 16:37.690
Um...

16:38.230 --> 16:42.770
The one who made it was Seimei's friend...

16:43.190 --> 16:45.270
...and I ate it with
one of my classmates.

16:45.270 --> 16:49.500
Oh, is that classmate a boy?

16:49.500 --> 16:50.710
A girl.

16:51.240 --> 16:53.280
Oh really, a girl.

16:53.280 --> 16:54.190
My rival...

16:54.190 --> 16:54.660
Huh?

16:55.410 --> 16:57.290
Oh, nothing.

16:57.290 --> 16:58.870
Eat up!

16:58.870 --> 17:00.660
There's also dessert!

17:02.290 --> 17:03.120
Okay!

17:04.960 --> 17:05.960
A beginning...

17:05.960 --> 17:06.790
...and the end.

17:06.790 --> 17:07.750
Everything...

17:07.750 --> 17:09.000
...yet nothing.

17:11.010 --> 17:13.210
We impart pain and suffering!

17:13.210 --> 17:15.180
We revert your existence
back to nothing!

17:16.310 --> 17:17.660
That's a good spell.

17:17.660 --> 17:20.590
Revert your existence back to nothing...

17:20.590 --> 17:21.890
Really good.

17:21.910 --> 17:23.070
Restraint! Take his freedom away!

17:24.060 --> 17:24.770
Get him!

17:26.820 --> 17:27.650
Release!

17:27.650 --> 17:28.770
Solidify!

17:29.280 --> 17:30.860
I see. He's fast.

17:30.860 --> 17:34.150
I heard you can endure a lot.

17:34.150 --> 17:35.610
Maybe you like pain.

17:37.240 --> 17:38.410
Of course not.

17:39.290 --> 17:40.660
I wonder...

17:40.660 --> 17:41.910
We'll see.

17:53.470 --> 17:54.670
Ritsuka.

17:55.890 --> 18:00.750
I'm a little relieved that
you made all sorts of friends.

18:02.940 --> 18:04.600
You like them, right?

18:06.400 --> 18:07.520
Who knows...

18:07.520 --> 18:08.690
"Who knows"?

18:08.690 --> 18:10.940
You're friends with them
because you like them, right?

18:11.900 --> 18:14.900
I think they like you.

18:15.780 --> 18:20.180
I don't like to be
told that they like me.

18:20.950 --> 18:26.920
I don't really know what
it means to like somebody.

18:26.920 --> 18:32.440
If Ritsuka disappears suddenly,
your friends will all be sad.

18:33.380 --> 18:35.490
I think that's what
liking somebody means.

18:36.390 --> 18:38.270
I like you.

18:45.900 --> 18:47.100
Doesn't it hurt?

18:47.100 --> 18:49.020
Scream if it hurts.

18:49.020 --> 18:50.440
Otherwise it's boring.

18:52.360 --> 18:53.690
I'm used to pain.

18:56.620 --> 19:00.400
Soubi, you can't cry out.

19:00.400 --> 19:01.660
Yes, sir.

19:01.660 --> 19:02.780
Get used to it.

19:03.660 --> 19:05.540
Don't be afraid of pain.

19:05.830 --> 19:07.750
You can endure it.

19:08.090 --> 19:10.110
Clench your teeth.

19:10.110 --> 19:11.790
Yes, sir.

19:14.130 --> 19:15.130
Clench your teeth.

19:17.210 --> 19:18.510
I can endure it.

19:18.970 --> 19:20.680
What's that spell?

19:20.680 --> 19:22.810
He's using self-hypnosis.
You've heard of it before.

19:22.810 --> 19:25.810
Yeah, but it's my first time
seeing somebody actually doing it.

19:25.810 --> 19:27.100
It gets on my nerves.

19:27.160 --> 19:27.850
Now!

19:28.480 --> 19:31.620
Attack! Run like lightning!

19:33.570 --> 19:35.710
Show us your pain!

19:36.530 --> 19:39.360
Zero doesn't have a sense of pain.

19:40.410 --> 19:44.830
Zero is Professor Nagisa's creation,
the man-made painless series.

19:45.620 --> 19:49.250
Because they don't feel pain,
they'll take extreme measures in a fight.

19:50.250 --> 19:52.150
But she's mistaken.

19:52.800 --> 19:55.040
Pain is a warning signal.

19:55.040 --> 19:57.460
It's also a shield to defend your body.

19:57.460 --> 20:00.970
Pain is proof that you're alive.

20:01.890 --> 20:05.190
Creating a Sentouki with no sense of
pain through genetic manipulation...

20:05.600 --> 20:09.070
For some reason,
they're all named Zero.

20:09.610 --> 20:13.350
An imitation. The only thing in this
world that doesn't have a name...

20:14.570 --> 20:16.350
...is called fate.

20:16.700 --> 20:19.100
You can never change fate.

20:19.100 --> 20:21.100
Resign to it.

20:21.100 --> 20:23.200
Be controlled by it.

20:23.200 --> 20:25.390
That's your fate...

20:25.390 --> 20:28.930
Fight to protect your Sacrifice.

20:30.830 --> 20:31.920
Does it hurt?

20:32.500 --> 20:34.120
I will not lose.

20:34.120 --> 20:35.530
What is this, false courage?

20:35.530 --> 20:38.550
I'm omnipotent,
and nothing is impossible.

20:38.550 --> 20:39.420
I'm invincible!

20:39.420 --> 20:40.840
A power-up spell!

20:40.840 --> 20:41.800
How fun.

20:41.800 --> 20:43.900
Even more annoying!

20:45.090 --> 20:48.680
Tear! Rupture his skin
in countless places!

20:51.940 --> 20:53.350
Like a red flower...

20:57.240 --> 20:58.630
See you next week.

21:04.910 --> 21:07.210
Aw, Ritsuka...

21:08.230 --> 21:09.950
If I were 20 years younger!

21:25.100 --> 21:26.050
Beautiful...

21:28.020 --> 21:29.760
What a beautiful image...

21:29.760 --> 21:34.730
To be continued...

21:30.970 --> 21:40.520
Setsunasa no kagiri made dakishimete mo

21:30.970 --> 21:40.520
Even if I hold you with all my suffering,

21:41.320 --> 21:50.830
itsu made mo hitotsu ni wa narenakute

21:41.320 --> 21:50.830
we still can't be one.

21:51.410 --> 22:01.340
Yasashisa yori fukai basho de fureau no wa itami dake

21:51.410 --> 22:01.340
The only thing that we can feel deep within besides kindness is pain,

22:01.750 --> 22:09.340
futari wo musunde kudasai

22:01.750 --> 22:09.340
so please, bind the two of us together.

22:11.890 --> 22:16.730
Bokura wa mou yume wo minai

22:11.890 --> 22:16.730
We no longer dream anymore,

22:16.730 --> 22:21.860
tomadoinagara te wo totte

22:16.730 --> 22:21.860
when you're wavering, take my hand

22:22.150 --> 22:31.070
zankoku na yoake no hou e arukidasu

22:22.150 --> 22:31.070
as we tread towards the cruel light of dawn.

22:32.200 --> 22:42.210
Hontou no kotoba wa kitto hontou no sekai no dokoka

22:32.200 --> 22:42.210
I'm sure real words are somewhere in the real world.

22:42.540 --> 22:51.430
Bokura no mukuchi na yoru ni hisonderu

22:42.540 --> 22:51.430
They lurk in the shadows of our silent nights.

22:51.800 --> 22:56.930
Ima mo kitto

22:51.800 --> 22:56.930
Surely, even now...

23:00.690 --> 23:04.020
Slimy, slimy, slimy...

23:04.020 --> 23:05.290
Slimy?

23:05.290 --> 23:07.530
What is this strange dream?

23:07.530 --> 23:10.160
How long are you going
to sleep? You're such a child.

23:10.660 --> 23:11.830
Agatsuma!

23:11.830 --> 23:13.790
Wait, this slimy thing is...

23:13.790 --> 23:14.950
Blood? Is it blood?

23:15.270 --> 23:17.290
It's my tears.

23:17.290 --> 23:18.210
Liar!

23:18.630 --> 23:20.880
Tale seven, Tearless.

23:20.880 --> 23:23.850
I doubt you've ever cried before!
